# Coding Conventions

- Match existing naming, file layout, and import style
- Prefer extending shared utilities over copy-paste
- Keep functions focused; avoid god-objects
- Do not silence type errors (`any`, `@ts-ignore`, bare `except`) without cause
- Fail loudly with actionable errors; no empty catch blocks
- Comments only for non-obvious intent; no narrating comments
- Config via env/settings modules already used by the project
- New dependency requires: why, alternatives considered, and blast radius

Full guide: `docs/conventions/coding.md`
